-- הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — הכנסת טכנולוגיות חדשות (10.1.2018): a special
-- collective agreement between the State (by the wages commissioner or the
-- acting Civil Service Commissioner), the National Insurance Institute and
-- the Employment Service, and the New General Histadrut with the Histadrut
-- of State Employees. It adds to §17 of the public-sector framework of
-- 18.4.2016 ("הסכם 2016", imported), which declared the Histadrut for new
-- technologies and made a dispute over them need the approval of its
-- coordination and execution committee: the Histadrut supports the changes
-- the employers ask for in developing, bringing in or embedding a new
-- technology ("שינוי בעניין טכנולוגי", §1.1); where the change involves no
-- outsourcing, no dismissals, no harm to the terms of employment and no
-- other circumstance the chair of the trade-union division thinks bears on
-- the employees, no dispute is declared, no measure that delays it is taken,
-- and the employees help and cooperate; otherwise each side keeps its claims
-- (§1.2); a dispute over such a change needs the committee's approval, and
-- the chair accompanies its resolution in person as needed (§1.3).
--
-- Whom it covers: it has no clause of coverage. It is a special agreement
-- (the Collective Agreements Law, §2(1), imported: it says so on its face
-- and is made for three named employers), so by §15 it reaches the
-- employees of those employers of the kinds it includes — and the
-- organisations that made it for the employees are the two Histadruts, the
-- representative organisations of the employees it is made for (§2(1)). It
-- covers no teaching employee: a teacher, whoever employs him, is
-- represented by הסתדרות המורים or ארגון המורים, neither of which signed
-- it. The corpus holds no teachers' instrument on
-- new technologies or on a dispute over one (a sweep for "טכנולוגיות
-- חדשות", "שינוי בעניין טכנולוגי", "הכנסת טכנולוג" and "מיקור חוץ" finds
-- only the public-sector frameworks of 2016, 2020 and 2023 and this one;
-- every other "טכנולוגי" in the corpus is a subject taught or a teacher's
-- training, and the September 2013 agreement's "באמצעים טכנולוגיים שונים"
-- is a way of reporting attendance, not a change in the work), so no round
-- is held for it. The framework of 17.7.2023 takes its place for the
-- employers that signed that one (§78(ד) there) and imports this file. It
-- speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT `2016-04-18_framework-agreement_public-sector`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — הכנסת טכנולוגיות חדשות (10.1.2018)`

@desc The parties the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 gives a duty to.
DECLARE `technologies party of 10.1.2018` IS ONE OF
    `the Histadrut, of 10.1.2018`
    `the employees, of 10.1.2018`

DECLARE `technologies action of 10.1.2018` IS ONE OF
    `support the technological changes the employers ask for, of 10.1.2018`
    `declare a dispute or take measures that delay a technological change, of 10.1.2018`
    `help and cooperate in a technological change as the employer requires, of 10.1.2018`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The registration stamp: registered on 16.9.2019, number 169/2019, by the chief labour relations officer; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 The Histadrut's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 A recital: the parties see importance in raising the productivity of work; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p17 A recital: the parties reached further understandings on the subject, set out below; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p18 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.
-- akn:art_1 The heading of §1: bringing in new technologies.
-- akn:conclusions The agreement's sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 "In witness whereof the parties signed"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The corpus's note that the signatures stand here; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The signature block of the State and the New General Histadrut; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 The signature line of the National Insurance Institute; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p4 The signature line of the Employment Service; no rule.

-- ¶2: it is a special collective agreement, as it says on its face and as
-- the law tells one apart: it is made for particular employers.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 is made for particular employers` MEANS TRUE

`the kind of the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018` MEANS
    `the kind of the collective agreement` `the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 is made for particular employers`

#ASSERT `the kind of the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018` EQUALS `a special collective agreement`

-- ¶3: signed on 10.1.2018 (the day and month written in by hand).
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the technologies agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2018

-- ¶5–¶7: the employers ("המעסיקים"): the State, by the wages commissioner
-- (Eran Yaakov) or the acting Civil Service Commissioner (Ehud Prawer);
-- the National Insurance Institute; the Employment Service.
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7
`the employers that signed the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018` MEANS
    LIST "מדינת ישראל", "המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שירות התעסוקה"

-- ¶11: for the employees, the New General Histadrut (by its chairman and
-- the chairman of the trade-union division) and the Histadrut of State
-- Employees ("ההסתדרות").
@ref akn:preamble/p11
`the organisations that signed the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 for the employees` MEANS
    LIST "הסתדרות העובדים הכללית החדשה", "הסתדרות עובדי המדינה"

-- ¶14: the framework of 18.4.2016 ("הסכם 2016"), amended since; ¶16: its
-- §17 anchored understandings on new technologies — imported.
@ref akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p16
`the agreement the technologies agreement adds to was signed on` MEANS `the 2016 framework agreement was signed on`

#ASSERT `the agreement the technologies agreement adds to was signed on` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 4 2016
#ASSERT `the Histadrut cooperates in new technologies`

§§ `מי שההסכם חל עליו`

-- The agreement has no clause of coverage, and the law answers whom a
-- special agreement reaches (§15): an employee of an employer that is a
-- party, of the kinds it includes. The kinds are those of the employees
-- the organisations that made it represent (§2(1): a special agreement is
-- made with "the representative organisation of the employees to whom it
-- will apply"), so an employee is in it where he is employed by one of the
-- three and one of the two Histadruts represents him.
@desc An employee, as far as the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 asks whether it reaches him.
DECLARE `technologies employee of 10.1.2018` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the technologies agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `represented by the Histadrut or the Histadrut of State Employees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN e IS A `technologies employee of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
DECIDE `the technologies employee, as the law asks` e IS
    `employee a collective agreement may reach` WITH
        `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the technologies agreement`
        `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS FALSE
        `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS FALSE
        `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS FALSE
        `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS e's `represented by the Histadrut or the Histadrut of State Employees`
        `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS TRUE

GIVEN e IS A `technologies employee of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 covers` e IF
    `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `the kind of the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018` (`the technologies employee, as the law asks` e)

`a clerk of the State in January 2018` MEANS `technologies employee of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the technologies agreement` IS TRUE
    `represented by the Histadrut or the Histadrut of State Employees` IS TRUE

`a teacher of the State in January 2018` MEANS `technologies employee of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the technologies agreement` IS TRUE
    `represented by the Histadrut or the Histadrut of State Employees` IS FALSE

`a clerk of a local authority in January 2018` MEANS `technologies employee of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the technologies agreement` IS FALSE
    `represented by the Histadrut or the Histadrut of State Employees` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 covers` `a clerk of the State in January 2018`
#ASSERT NOT `the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 covers` `a teacher of the State in January 2018`
#ASSERT NOT `the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018 covers` `a clerk of a local authority in January 2018`

§§ `1 הכנסת טכנולוגיות חדשות`

-- §1.1: the Histadrut declares for bringing in new technologies and will
-- support the changes the employers ask for in developing (including the
-- characterising of needs and work processes), bringing in or embedding a
-- new technology ("שינוי בעניין טכנולוגי").
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-1
`supporting the technological changes of 10.1.2018` MEANS
    PARTY `the Histadrut, of 10.1.2018`
    MUST  `support the technological changes the employers ask for, of 10.1.2018`

@desc A technological change, as far as §1.2 of the agreement of 10.1.2018 asks.
DECLARE `technological change of 10.1.2018` HAS
    `puts work out to outsourcing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves dismissing employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `harms the employees' terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bears on the employees, in the trade-union division chair's view` IS A BOOLEAN @desc another circumstance in labour relations that the chair of the trade-union division thinks bears on the employees

-- §1.2: where the change involves none of (א) outsourcing, (ב) dismissals,
-- (ג) harm to the terms of employment, (ד) another circumstance in labour
-- relations that the chair of the trade-union division thinks bears on the
-- employees — ¶2: no dispute is declared and no organisational measure that
-- delays the technology is taken, and the employees help and cooperate in
-- all that is needed within their work (answering questions, taking part in
-- instruction and training, making the changes and adjustments the new
-- technology needs) as the employer requires. ¶3: in any other case each
-- side keeps its claims.
-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: 1.2 names dismissals only as a change
-- the industrial peace over new technologies does not cover; it gives or
-- asks no notice, so it rules nothing the law puts a floor under.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-2 akn:art_1__para_1-2__subpara_a akn:art_1__para_1-2__subpara_b akn:art_1__para_1-2__subpara_c akn:art_1__para_1-2__subpara_d
GIVEN t IS A `technological change of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` t IF
    NOT (   t's `puts work out to outsourcing`
         OR t's `involves dismissing employees`
         OR t's `harms the employees' terms of employment`
         OR t's `bears on the employees, in the trade-union division chair's view`)

@ref akn:art_1__para_1-2/p2
GIVEN t IS A `technological change of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `technologies party of 10.1.2018` `technologies action of 10.1.2018`
DECIDE `no dispute that delays a technological change of 10.1.2018` t IS
    IF `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` t
    THEN PARTY `the Histadrut, of 10.1.2018`
         SHANT `declare a dispute or take measures that delay a technological change, of 10.1.2018`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN t IS A `technological change of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `technologies party of 10.1.2018` `technologies action of 10.1.2018`
DECIDE `the employees cooperate in a technological change of 10.1.2018` t IS
    IF `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` t
    THEN PARTY `the employees, of 10.1.2018`
         MUST  `help and cooperate in a technological change as the employer requires, of 10.1.2018`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:art_1__para_1-2/p3
GIVEN t IS A `technological change of 10.1.2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each side keeps its claims over a technological change of 10.1.2018` t IF
    NOT `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` t

-- §1.3: declaring a dispute over a technological change needs the approval
-- of the Histadrut's coordination and execution committee — as §17 of the
-- framework of 2016 has it, imported; the chair of the trade-union division
-- accompanies its resolution in person, as needed. A dispute may be
-- declared only over a change §1.2 leaves open, and then only with that
-- approval.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-3
GIVEN t IS A `technological change of 10.1.2018`
      `the coordination and execution committee approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute over a technological change of 10.1.2018 may be declared` t `the coordination and execution committee approved` IF
        `each side keeps its claims over a technological change of 10.1.2018` t
    AND `a dispute over new technologies may be declared` `the coordination and execution committee approved`

`the trade-union division's chair accompanies the resolution in person, of 10.1.2018` MEANS TRUE

-- A change that only brings in new software: free of disputes, and the
-- employees cooperate. One that dismisses employees, or one the chair
-- thinks bears on them, is not: each side keeps its claims, and a dispute
-- may be declared over it with the committee's approval and not without.
`a new system with no other effect, of 10.1.2018` MEANS `technological change of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `puts work out to outsourcing` IS FALSE
    `involves dismissing employees` IS FALSE
    `harms the employees' terms of employment` IS FALSE
    `bears on the employees, in the trade-union division chair's view` IS FALSE

`a new system that dismisses employees, of 10.1.2018` MEANS `technological change of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `puts work out to outsourcing` IS FALSE
    `involves dismissing employees` IS TRUE
    `harms the employees' terms of employment` IS FALSE
    `bears on the employees, in the trade-union division chair's view` IS FALSE

`a new system the chair thinks bears on the employees, of 10.1.2018` MEANS `technological change of 10.1.2018` WITH
    `puts work out to outsourcing` IS FALSE
    `involves dismissing employees` IS FALSE
    `harms the employees' terms of employment` IS FALSE
    `bears on the employees, in the trade-union division chair's view` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` `a new system with no other effect, of 10.1.2018`
#ASSERT NOT `a dispute over a technological change of 10.1.2018 may be declared` `a new system with no other effect, of 10.1.2018` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a technological change of 10.1.2018 is free of disputes` `a new system that dismisses employees, of 10.1.2018`
#ASSERT `a dispute over a technological change of 10.1.2018 may be declared` `a new system that dismisses employees, of 10.1.2018` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a dispute over a technological change of 10.1.2018 may be declared` `a new system that dismisses employees, of 10.1.2018` FALSE
#ASSERT `each side keeps its claims over a technological change of 10.1.2018` `a new system the chair thinks bears on the employees, of 10.1.2018`
